{
  "record_id": "016",
  "problem": "Channel additivity violations",
  "collection": "Original research investigation",
  "summary": "The balancing side channel need not have constant dimension or constant additive qubit cost.",
  "review_status": "source_reviewed",
  "review_note": "No open interpretation blocker was recorded in the preceding source review. This is not a new independent mathematical verification.",
  "original": {
    "excerpt": "A Holevo pair gap g for finite-dimensional channels N and M can, after balancing their one-shot\n  Holevo quantities within one bit by a bounded classical side channel and taking T = N' direct-sum\n  M', be converted into chi(T tensor T) - 2 chi(T) at least g - log_2(9/4), with only constant\n  additive qubit overhead.",
    "context": "The proposed conversion balances the one-shot Holevo information of two channels by adding a classical side channel of size K, then forms a direct sum. The node was marked CONJECTURED; this record concerns the overly strong dimension-overhead clause, not a falsely certified final theorem.",
    "locator": "Proof-node creation event, 2026-08-30T01:21:04.780Z, JSONL line 3188"
  },
  "witness": {
    "explanation": "The balancing side channel need not have constant dimension or constant additive qubit cost.",
    "evidence": "If the Holevo quantities differ by Delta, balancing them within one bit requires |log2 K-Delta|<1, so log2 K>Delta-1. Taking channels with Holevo quantities log2 d and 0 makes the required overhead grow as log2 d. The final direct sum itself adds at most one qubit, but that does not erase the preceding balancing cost. The equal-Holevo special case avoids this cost.",
    "scope": "statement_false"
  },
  "archived_witness_excerpt": null,
  "visible_reasoning": {
    "availability_description": "pair-to-self 的摘要只是主题标题，没有目标维数成本的推导。",
